2026-09-23 — stable integer comparison-selection and dereference arm typing.

RED: three failing CLI tests, zero Rust compilation errors. Ordinary minimum
reloads its two operands (4 loads rather than 2). Independently, C-HIR rejects
the conditional's integer dereference arm type with E3007, masking actual
E3001/E3004/E3009/E3011 execution diagnostics. A second one-assertion RED
exposes the unnecessary branch/join after the compared values are retained.

GREEN: shared integer type classification obtains a dereference's canonical
pointee without evaluating its operand. Both conditional arms receive their
normal conversions; unselected null pointers are not accessed and pointer
updates occur only once on the selected path.

Optimized lowering matches bounded, typed, structurally identical integer
operands and reuses the comparison's already evaluated/common-converted values.
It selects with b ^ ((a ^ b) & -zext(predicate)), using existing total EvoIR
bit operations rather than inventing C signed arithmetic or a new instruction.
Both operands have already been semantically read; this does not speculate
general conditional arms or waive poison/access/arithmetic obligations.
Symbol, projection, index type and qualifier identities are retained; volatile,
atomic, calls, updates, allocations and register-bound inputs do not match.
There is no validator weakening, cross-block use or EqSat allowlist expansion.

Six CLI regressions cover all six comparisons, swapped selection, scalar and
128-bit values, mixed signedness, narrow promotion, array/record places,
surrounding live values/effects, unselected expressions and retained errors.
C-HIR/EvoIR execution at O0/O2, MIR validation/execution and emission pass.
Sealed ARM64 GCC 14.2.0-19 / Clang 19.1.7 / EvoCC at O0/O2 all exit zero:
6/6 native controls. Network is disabled; the original sealed image is reused.

Original LLVM LARGE floyd-warshall uses its frozen source SHA and command,
existing projector/sysroot, timeit limits, appended exit status and upstream
HashProgramOutput/fpcmp contract. Result remains TIMEOUT 124 at 60 seconds;
timeit kills its monitored process. No output PASS is inferred. Core function
instructions are 160 before / 143 with retained branch / 108 with bit selection.
No reference object, kernel Image, module or full-campaign receipt was replaced.
The local test/replay directory is less than 1 MiB; no source tree was copied.

Final affected gate against 03fa009: 1819 PASS, 0 FAIL, 3 historical ignored,
212 result groups in eight crates. Clippy --all-targets -D warnings, workspace
fmt, renderer and diff checks PASS. The earlier retained-branch gate is a
separate run and is not counted again.
The rebuilt release emits byte-identical assembly for the unchanged original.
